      "name": "standalone_without_hitched_falls_back_to_axle_estimate",
      "requires": ["predictive_truck_estimate"],
      "_note": "Regression case for a real bug, fixed 2026-08-21 in both Python (compute_breakdown) and Kotlin (Breakdown.kt): a stand-alone reading with no real hitched (steer+drive) reading used to be treated the same as a real hitched+standalone pair, silently producing the wrong trailer total (11,380, the unadjusted axle reading) instead of the correct 14,225 axle-based estimate. Its Trailer Total row is correct in both platforms as of the 2026-08-21 fix, but this case is still tagged as requiring predictive_truck_estimate because its Tow Vehicle Total row's expected values (the standalone-only predictive branch) also depend on that capability, which Python already has and Kotlin doesn't yet (Round 2) - Python's own oracle bakes both capabilities into this input combination together, so there's no way to isolate just the trailer fix here without changing the scenario.",
      "truck": {"gvwr_lb": 14000, "front_gawr_lb": 6000, "rear_gawr_lb": 9500, "standalone_weight_lb": 10000},
      "trailer": {"gvwr_lb": 12500, "gawr_per_axle_lb": 6000},
      "scale": {"trailer_axle_lb": 11380},
